    "title": "David Wagner's Home in Photos - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Abby Montanez ,\n8 hours ago The creative compound is on the market for $3.6 million. Click here for the full story .\n1.\nThe Pueblo-inspired contemporary compound spans 1.43 acres.\n2.\nA minimalist sculpture garden with a water feature.\n3.\nSoaring wood-beam ceilings and a fireplace anchor the main living room.\n4.\nThe kitchen.\n5.\nA dining area adjoins the kitchen.\n6.\nOne of the bedrooms.\n7.\nThe primary bath.\n8.\nAnother bedroom.\n9.\nThere’s also a casita for guests.\n10.\nIt includes a linear kitchen and a bedroom.\n11.\nOpposite the kitchen is a built-in bench for dining.\n12.\nThe art studio.\n13.\nAn library and lounge area off the studio.\n14.\nA library pavilion serves as the home of Friends of the Sky, the nonprofit foundation established to preserve artist Tal Streeter’s work, writings, and archives.\n15.\nIt spans two floors.\n16.\nAn exterior staircase climbs to a roof terrace.\nView Full Gallery (16 Photos)",
    "summary": "8 hours ago The creative compound is on the market for $3.6 million. The Pueblo-inspired contemporary compound spans 1.43 acres. Soaring wood-beam ceilings and a fireplace anchor the main living room. Opposite the kitchen is a built-in bench for dining. A library pavilion serves as the home of Friends of the Sky, the nonprofit foundation established to preserve artist Tal Streeter’s work, writings, and archives.",
